      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's a good start, but it feels a bit... wordy in the second half. the \"Prestige Sentiment Engine\" is flagging it at a 42, which is okay, but I'm worried the client will find the ending a bit too flowery and lose the actual specs of the place.\n\ncan you try another version? i need it to be punchier. try to keep the factual info (the sq ft, the marble, the pool) very prominent, but let's see if we can get that engine score up closer to 60 or 70 without it looking like a total mess. just try to weave the prestige words in more naturally so it doesn't feel like we're just listing adjectives.",
      "source": "evaluator"
